Task: Arcs (Phase 2, Track foundation-core_20260918)

Red phase: tests first, failed on the missing module. Green phase: eight new
tests pass, twenty-six in total.

What the tests pin down:
- The bent path passes exactly through its start and end.
- The bending point pulls the path towards itself without being touched: the
  middle lands a quarter of the way between the straight chord and that point,
  which is the property people get wrong when they assume the curve reaches it.
- A bending point placed on the straight line produces a straight line, so the
  general case degrades correctly.
- The throw is zero at both ends, peaks at exactly its height halfway, is
  symmetric, and never exceeds its height.
- Time outside the range is clamped rather than extrapolated.

Design note:
The throw returns a height, not a coordinate. Whether up means a larger or
smaller number depends on where the value is consumed, and deciding that here
would be this layer knowing something about the application that it must not.
